       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine's labeled maximum is 10 mg once daily for adults, and 50 mg is five times that. At that dose, the risks include severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdoses can also cause prolonged shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg PO daily.** This is the maximum dose. The usual start is 2.5\u20135 mg daily, titrated up.\n- **Enter a lower starting dose**, such as 5 mg PO daily, if the patient is new to the drug.\n- **Add a second agent** if 10 mg isn't controlling blood pressure. Examples are an ACE inhibitor, an ARB, or a thiazide-type diuretic.\n\nIf 50 mg was a typo, tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it. If you meant something else, such as a different drug or a different unit, let me know."
